# Agent orchestration index

Subagents live in **`.cursor/agents/`**. **Parent** picks Feature vs Direct per `.cursor/rules/issue-tracking.mdc`, then runs `.cursor/rules/orchestration.mdc`.

| Subagent | When |
|--|--|
| **planner** | **Feature** track after discuss + size - issue spec + rubric; sync GitHub issue |
| **designer** | Briefing §17 gaps or L/XL IA changes - HTML wireframes; skip when design-index covers the screen ([design-when](design-when.mdc)) |
| **architect** | Stack, ADR drafts, unresolved forks |
| **generator** | Feature implement (+ design HTML when present); TDD; `generator-state.md` on `development` |
| **code-reviewer** | Optional light diff - skip Direct/micro-S/many S; M+ or risk |
| **api-reviewer** | Huma `/api/v1` handlers, webhooks, SSE |
| **mcp-reviewer** | MCP tools, schemas, auth |
| **database-reviewer** | goose migrations, sqlc, SQLite constraints |
| **security-reviewer** | Auth, secrets, OWASP surfaces |
| **frontend-evaluator** | Live UI vs design-index / wireframe + rubric |
| **performance-evaluator** | Footprint / Lighthouse when rubric requires |
| **doc-updater** | **After** all other required reviewers PASS |

**Direct track:** usually no subagent fan-out - parent implements on `development`.

Reviewer selection: `.cursor/rules/reviewer-defaults.mdc` + issue rubric (Feature).

All Feature reviewers write to `docs/project/feedback/<issue>/<type>-i<iter>.md`.

Skills: `.cursor/skills/README.md` — start with **dockyrd-dev** for implementation.
